// ============================================================================
// waterfall.kn — TurboKain 16: Science-Grade Waterfall & Diagnostic HUD (v0.3.0)
//
// Generates publication-grade, multi-panel 1920x1080 diagnostic PNG images
// directly through native Kain. Designed for both human interstellar research
// and multimodal vision LLMs to inspect the full structure of raw radio scans.
//
// v0.3.0 SCIENCE CORE (industry-standard upgrades):
//   * FULL-COVERAGE block-averaged STFT: every display row integrates ALL of
//     its time segment (linear power mean over N FFTs), not one sparse probe.
//     Sparse 0.7%-sampling is gone; transients cannot fall between needles.
//   * LINEAR-THEN-dB discipline: power is averaged in linear units and only
//     then converted to dB (radiometer-correct). Averaging dB was a bias.
//   * HALF-SPECTRUM display (512 unique bins, BW = fs/2): real-valued input
//     no longer renders its conjugate mirror as a second sky signal.
//   * PERCENTILE dynamic range (p5/p99 over the full STFT plane), so the same
//     noise maps to the same colors across files.
//   * SK thresholds derived from M (3-sigma ~= 6/sqrt(M)), not fixed +-0.2.
//   * drift.csv parsed with CORRECT absolute-Hz columns (freq_hz,drift_x100,
//     sigma_x100,kind); up to 3 in-band candidates overlaid with physically
//     correct slope pixels = drift_rate * duration / bandwidth.
//   * Card 6 reads EVERY lane CSV in --dir (sk/xeno/boxcar-pulse/drift/jerk/
//     frame-fold/lag/fam/scint); nothing hardcoded except the honest
//     STANDALONE cadence note for single-beam runs.
//   * Card 7 harvests evidence.csv with per-tool unit handling (DRIFT/JERK
//     absolute MHz; FAM/FOLD/FRAME/LAG x100->Hz; PULSE/SK/XENO/SCINT class).
//
// Multi-panel layout:
//   * Header Banner: Target, Center Freq, Sample Rate, Duration, Obs Time
//   * Panel 1: Integrated Power Spectrum P(f) with median noise baseline,
//              detection threshold, and peak callout arrows (aligned with WF)
//   * Panel 2: Main 2D Dynamic Waterfall Heatmap P(t, f) with Turbo/Inferno
//              colormap, time/frequency ticks, and authentic candidate drift lines
//   * Panel 3: Time-Domain Total Power Envelope P(t) showing burst transients
//   * Panel 4: Spectral Kurtosis SK(f) showing Gaussian baseline & RFI excision
//   * Panel 5: Observation & Statistical Telemetry HUD Card
//   * Panel 6: Multi-Instrument Pipeline Verdicts Matrix (SK, Xeno, Boxcar,
//              Drift, Jerk, Frame, Lag, Fam, Scint, Cadence)
//   * Panel 7: Ranked Candidate Hit Table with exact parameters (harvested live)
//   * Panel 8: Calibrated dB Colorbar Scale (percentile-anchored)
//   * Footer: Provenance (input FFTs/coverage/scale) & Z3/CBMC Receipt
//
// USAGE:
//   core waterfall --in <scan.f32> [--out <scan.png>] [--dir <reports_dir>]
//                  [--fs <hz>] [--target <name>] [--freq-mhz <f0>] [--cmap <turbo|inferno>]
//   core waterfall --prove
// ============================================================================

